["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A covey goes up in one second. You name the bird by its plume, its face and its size before the gun moves, or you do not shoot.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three small upland birds drawn to scale by weight. California quail, 140 to 230 grams, curled black plume. Gray partridge or Hun, 300 to 500 grams, orange face and chestnut horseshoe. Chukar, 538 to 765 grams, red bill and legs and a black necklace. Weights from Audubon, 75 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Three small upland birds, to scale</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"150\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(75 130) scale(1.0 1.0)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(195 128) scale(1.35 1.35)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(320 124) scale(1.6 1.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/><path d=\"M-20 -2 L-30 -4 L-28 5 Z\" fill=\"#8b6f4a\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 v12 M-3 -7 v13 M2 -7 v13 M7 -6 v12\" stroke=\"#2f2f2f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9fa4a8\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 q6 -2 13 2 q-4 10 -11 10\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"#f3ead8\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M26 -14 l5 1 l-5 3 Z\" fill=\"#d23b2a\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 8 M9 13 l2 8\" stroke=\"#d23b2a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g>\n<text x=\"75\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">California quail</text>\n<text x=\"75\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">140 to 230 g</text>\n<text x=\"75\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">curled plume</text>\n<text x=\"195\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gray partridge</text>\n<text x=\"195\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">300 to 500 g</text>\n<text x=\"195\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">orange face</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">538 to 765 g</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">black necklace</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Weights: Audubon field guide (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Three small upland birds share the South Okanagan: quail, chukar and gray partridge <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Quail is the smallest: 140 to 230 g <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this Masterclass covers</summary><ul><li>Ten chapters, one per session: the bird, the body, the senses, the mind, the year, the day, where they live, sign, how to hunt, and shot to table with the rules.</li><li>The quick version stays: <a href=\"#/s/upland-birds\">Quail, chukar, partridge, pheasant</a> and <a href=\"#/s/first-quail-trip\">Your first quail trip</a>.</li><li>Each chapter ends with memory hooks and a 5 question quiz. Chapter 10 has the one page cheat sheet.</li><li>Focus: California quail in the South Okanagan, Region 8. Chukar and gray partridge get their own screens where you might meet them.</li><li>Rules are only what the app's <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Rule Book</a> says. This Masterclass adds no new rules.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Large drawing of a male California quail with five numbered marks: 1 curled black plume, 2 black face outlined in white, 3 scaled belly, 4 white streaks on grey brown sides, 5 chestnut belly patch. Below, a small female: plain grey brown face and a small plume, no black face. 80 percent, Audubon and Cornell.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Male California quail: 5 marks</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(110 150) scale(3.0 3.0)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<line x1=\"156\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"201\" y2=\"61\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"205\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">1 Curled black plume</text>\n<line x1=\"125\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"201\" y2=\"93\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"205\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">2 Black face, white rim</text>\n<line x1=\"105\" y1=\"158\" x2=\"201\" y2=\"153\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"205\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">3 Scaled belly</text>\n<line x1=\"80\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"201\" y2=\"123\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"205\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">4 White side streaks</text>\n<line x1=\"95\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"201\" y2=\"183\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"205\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">5 Chestnut belly patch</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"222\" width=\"380\" height=\"66\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(50 262) scale(1.3 1.3)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-1 -6 5 -6 q-3 1 -3 6 Z\" fill=\"#4a4a4a\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"90\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Female: plain grey brown face,</text>\n<text x=\"90\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">small plume, no black face (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Curled black plume, black face rimmed in white <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Scaled belly with a chestnut patch, white streaks on the sides <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: male marks in full</summary><ul><li>Length 24 to 27 cm, wingspan 32 to 37 cm, weight 140 to 230 g (75%, Audubon).</li><li>The male's plume is six feathers that curl forward like a comma (85%, BC Breeding Bird Atlas).</li><li>Male: black face and throat edged with white, buff forehead, brown cap, blue grey breast, scaled belly with a chestnut centre patch <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Sides: grey brown with white streaks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>He walks with a nodding head, often in the open next to cover (75%, Audubon).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-quail-male-vernon.jpg\" alt=\"Male, Vernon: black face, white rim, big curled plume.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Male, Vernon: black face, white rim, big curled plume. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan D. Wilson, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:California_Quail_(Male).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-quail-female.jpg\" alt=\"Female: plain grey brown face, small plume, scaled belly.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Female: plain grey brown face, small plume, scaled belly. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan Vernon, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Callipepla_californica_-California,_USA_-female_and_chick-_8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-quail-pair.jpg\" alt=\"A pair. The female is plainer and smaller in the plume.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A pair. The female is plainer and smaller in the plume. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: BLM Nevada, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:California_Quail_Fallon_NV_(19978763835).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Both sexes carry a plume. Hers is smaller and brown <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>She has no black face and no white rim <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: female marks in full</summary><ul><li>Female: grey brown head and back, no black and white face, smaller plume, the same scaled belly (80%, Audubon and Edgewood notes).</li><li>In a flushing covey you rarely see the face. Sex does not matter for the bag in Region 8: the row is \"QUAIL\", 10 a day (99%, Rule Book).</li><li>Tip: on the ground, count black faces to guess how many cocks are in a covey.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two quail wings compared. Young of the year: buff tips on the upper primary coverts and pointed outer flight feathers. Adult: plain grey covert tips and rounder outer feathers. 70 percent, from a 1963 Condor aging study, search preview. The tips show best in early season.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Young or adult? Check the wing</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Young of the year</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(22 110)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L120 -10 L150 20 L130 60 L20 50 Z\" fill=\"#9a9ca2\"/><path d=\"M100 -6 l40 30\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M108 -2 l40 28\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M116 2 l40 26\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M124 6 l40 24\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M132 10 l40 22\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"75\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e8c27a\"/><ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"7\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"85\" cy=\"7\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e8c27a\"/><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"95\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e8c27a\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"17\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"17\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e8c27a\"/><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"115\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#e8c27a\"/></g>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Buff tips on the</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">primary coverts</text>\n<text x=\"297\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Adult</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(217 110)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L120 -10 L150 20 L130 60 L20 50 Z\" fill=\"#9a9ca2\"/><path d=\"M100 -6 l40 30\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M108 -2 l40 28\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M116 2 l40 26\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M124 6 l40 24\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M132 10 l40 22\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"75\" cy=\"2\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"7\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"85\" cy=\"7\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"95\" cy=\"12\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"17\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"17\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#6d6f75\"/><ellipse cx=\"115\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"3\" ry=\"2.5\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/></g>\n<text x=\"297\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Plain grey tips,</text>\n<text x=\"297\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">rounder outer feathers</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aging clue from a 1963 study (70%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Count your young: a sign of a good hatch (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>In fall, most of a covey are young of the year <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Buff tips on the wing coverts mark a young bird <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: aging in full</summary><ul><li>Juvenile California quail keep buff coloured upper primary coverts and pointed outer flight feathers until their first full moult (70%, 1963 Condor aging study, search preview).</li><li>Hunters across North America use the buff covert tips to age quail of every species (60%, Project Upland, search preview).</li><li>Many young in your bag means a good hatch. A New Zealand study used the young share of the bag as an index of breeding success (65%, search preview).</li><li>By October the young look like small, dull females (Tip, 65%, from the quick lesson).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Grid of six birds, legal or not, from the app Rule Book. California quail, curled plume: yes, Region 8. Mountain quail, straight plume: no open season. Chukar, red bill and black necklace: yes, Regions 3 and 8. Gray partridge, orange face: yes, Regions 3 and 8. Pheasant cock, green head and white ring: yes, cocks only. Pheasant hen, brown with a long tail: never. 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Legal or not? From the Rule Book</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"36\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">California quail</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Curled plume</text>\n<rect x=\"34\" y=\"86\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, Region 8</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"36\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mountain quail</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Straight plume</text>\n<rect x=\"226\" y=\"86\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO season</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"113\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red bill, necklace</text>\n<rect x=\"34\" y=\"163\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, Regions 3, 8</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"113\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gray partridge</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange face</text>\n<rect x=\"226\" y=\"163\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, Regions 3, 8</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"190\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pheasant cock</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Green head, ring</text>\n<rect x=\"34\" y=\"240\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, cocks only</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"190\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pheasant hen</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brown, long tail</text>\n<rect x=\"226\" y=\"240\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NEVER</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Seasons: Rule Book (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-mountain-quail.jpg\" alt=\"Mountain quail: long straight plume, white bars on red sides. No open season.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Mountain quail: long straight plume, white bars on red sides. No open season. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Alan Schmierer, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountainquail_(cropped).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Straight plume? Mountain quail. No open season <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Brown bird with a long tail? Hen pheasant. Never legal <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: look alikes in full</summary><ul><li>Mountain quail: long straight plume, chestnut throat, broad white bars on red brown sides (80%, Audubon). The Rule Book: \"No open season on mountain quail.\" Region 1, page 21 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>The Region 8 row says only \"QUAIL\". The law behind it, the <a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/190_84_00\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunting Regulation</a>, Schedule 8, item 23, also says only \"QUAIL\" and names no kind (99%, BC Laws, current to 13 October 2026, checked 2026-10-17). My reading: the season is not limited to California quail <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Still shoot California quail only (Tip, from the <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8 Rule Book</a>).</li><li>Chukar and gray partridge: legal in Regions 3 and 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Pheasant: cocks only, Regions 2, 3 and 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Grouse flush from the same draws in September and October. Different rows, different limits (99%, Rule Book).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-chukar.jpg\" alt=\"Chukar: red bill and legs, black necklace, barred flanks.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Chukar: red bill and legs, black necklace, barred flanks. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Artemy Voikhansky, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chukar_partridge.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>538 to 765 g, red bill and legs, black necklace <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Sexes look alike. Young are duller <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: chukar marks in full</summary><ul><li>Length 34 to 38 cm, wingspan about 51 cm (75%, Audubon).</li><li>Sandy brown back, grey breast, buff belly. A black band runs from the forehead through the eye and down to a necklace around a cream throat <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Flanks: bold vertical bars of black, white and chestnut. Bill, legs and eye ring coral red <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Males are a little heavier. Juveniles are mottled grey brown without the sharp head and flank pattern <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Call: a loud, fast \"chuck chuck chukar\" from the rocks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Native to Asia. BC is the only Canadian province where it took hold (65%, BC Outdoors).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 414\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two birds, 80 percent. Chukar, 540 to 765 grams: black necklace, red bill and legs, sandy grey with barred flanks, the bigger bird. Grey partridge, the Hun, 300 to 500 grams: orange face, chestnut horseshoe on the belly, rusty tail, smaller and grey below.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"414\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar or grey partridge? (80%)</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"44\" width=\"384\" height=\"176\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\">Chukar</text>\n<text x=\"91.632\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">540 to 765 g</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"104\" cy=\"207.0\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#000\" opacity=\".1\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(104 148) scale(3.0)\"><path d=\"M-3 10 L-4 19 M-4 19 l-4 1 M-4 19 l3 1\" stroke=\"#d1342a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M5 10 L4 19 M4 19 l-4 1 M4 19 l3 1\" stroke=\"#d1342a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M14 -2 L26 -6 L25 3 L14 4z\" fill=\"#a39684\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"2\" cy=\"1\" rx=\"17\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#b2a796\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M2 -2 l-3 9\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M4 -2 l-3 9\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><path d=\"M7 -2 l-3 9\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M9 -2 l-3 9\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><path d=\"M12 -2 l-3 9\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M14 -2 l-3 9\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><path d=\"M-15 -3 C-17 -10 -15 -16 -9 -17 C-4 -17 -2 -13 -3 -8 C-6 -4 -10 -2 -15 -3z\" fill=\"#e6dcc8\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M-15 -12 C-12 -10 -9 -9 -6 -4 C-8 -2 -12 -2 -15 -3\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M-15 -12 L-20 -10.5 L-15 -9.5z\" fill=\"#d1342a\"/><circle cx=\"-11\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.4\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"126.4\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"275.175\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black necklace</text>\n<line x1=\"74\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"99.5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"74\" cy=\"130\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"119.0\" width=\"138.2\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"281.114\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red bill and legs</text>\n<line x1=\"47\" y1=\"116.5\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"132.5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"47\" cy=\"116.5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"152.0\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"288.818\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sandy grey, barred</text>\n<line x1=\"128\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"165.5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"128\" cy=\"154\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"185.0\" width=\"61.2\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"242.594\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bigger</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"228\" width=\"384\" height=\"176\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\">Grey partridge</text>\n<text x=\"155.96\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">300 to 500 g</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"104\" cy=\"382.4\" rx=\"51\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#000\" opacity=\".1\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(104 332) scale(2.55)\"><path d=\"M-3 10 L-4 19 M-4 19 l-4 1 M-4 19 l3 1\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M5 10 L4 19 M4 19 l-4 1 M4 19 l3 1\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M14 -2 L25 -5 L25 3 L14 4z\" fill=\"#b5652d\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"2\" cy=\"1\" rx=\"17\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#9b9a8e\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M-4 3 C-2 0 3 0 5 3 C3 7 -2 7 -4 3z\" fill=\"#7a3e1d\"/><path d=\"M4 -6 C8 -8 12 -6 15 -3\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M-15 -3 C-17 -10 -15 -16 -9 -17 C-4 -17 -2 -13 -3 -8 C-6 -4 -10 -2 -15 -3z\" fill=\"#d98a3d\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M-15 -12 L-19 -10.5 L-15 -9.5z\" fill=\"#8f8a7d\"/><circle cx=\"-11\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.4\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"270.0\" width=\"102.9\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"263.459\" y=\"289\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange face</text>\n<line x1=\"73.4\" y1=\"303.95\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"283.5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"73.4\" cy=\"303.95\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"303.0\" width=\"160.7\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"292.349\" y=\"322\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chestnut horseshoe</text>\n<line x1=\"104\" y1=\"339.65\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"316.5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"104\" cy=\"339.65\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"336.0\" width=\"85.9\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"254.952\" y=\"355\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rusty tail</text>\n<line x1=\"160.1\" y1=\"329.45\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"349.5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"160.1\" cy=\"329.45\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<rect x=\"212.0\" y=\"369.0\" width=\"162.9\" height=\"27.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"293.472\" y=\"388\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Smaller, grey below</text>\n<line x1=\"114.2\" y1=\"354.95\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"382.5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"114.2\" cy=\"354.95\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/bd-gray-partridge.jpg\" alt=\"A pair of Huns in a grain field: orange faces, chestnut bars on grey sides.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A pair of Huns in a grain field: orange faces, chestnut bars on grey sides. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Åsa Berndtsson, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rapph%C3%B6na_Grey_Partridge_(14334064297).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Orange face, chestnut horseshoe, rusty tail in flight <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>300 to 500 g. Flushes with a cackle <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: gray partridge marks in full</summary><ul><li>Length 30 to 33 cm, wingspan 50 to 56 cm (75%, Audubon).</li><li>Grey below, orange face and throat, chestnut belly patch, rusty outer tail feathers that flash on the flush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The chestnut patch is smaller on the female <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Call: a hoarse \"kee ah\"; a rapid cackle when flushed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The synopsis spells it \"GRAY (Hungarian) PARTRIDGE\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Hunters say <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Huns\">Huns</button>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of body weight in grams. California quail 140 to 230. Gray partridge 300 to 500. Chukar 538 to 765. Lengths: quail 24 to 27 centimetres, partridge 30 to 33, chukar 34 to 38. Audubon field guide, 75 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Weight in grams (Audubon, 75%)</text>\n<text x=\"112\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Quail</text><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"60\" width=\"264\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/><rect x=\"166.2\" y=\"60\" width=\"29.700000000000017\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"199.9\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">24 to 27 cm</text>\n<text x=\"112\" y=\"121\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Hun</text><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"105\" width=\"264\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/><rect x=\"219.0\" y=\"105\" width=\"66.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"289.0\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">30 to 33 cm</text>\n<text x=\"112\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chukar</text><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"150\" width=\"264\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/><rect x=\"297.54\" y=\"150\" width=\"74.91000000000003\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#a33b2a\"/><text x=\"293.54\" y=\"167\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">34 to 38 cm</text>\n<line x1=\"120\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"384\" y2=\"196\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"202\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"120.0\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><line x1=\"186.0\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"186.0\" y2=\"202\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"186.0\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">200</text><line x1=\"252.0\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"252.0\" y2=\"202\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"252.0\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">400</text><line x1=\"318.0\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"318.0\" y2=\"202\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"318.0\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">600</text><line x1=\"384.0\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"384.0\" y2=\"202\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"384.0\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">800</text>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grams</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"252\" width=\"380\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"277\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A quail weighs about as much as a cup of water</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Quail 140 to 230 g. Hun 300 to 500 g. Chukar 538 to 765 g <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A quail is about the weight of a cup of water (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why size matters</summary><ul><li>On the flush, size and wingbeat help name the bird: a quail is half a Hun and a third of a chukar (75%, from Audubon weights).</li><li>Small bird, small shot: lead 7.5 or 8 are standard for quail (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife). See chapter 10.</li><li>About 160 g is a typical BC quail (65%, BC Outdoors).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline of quail and chukar in BC. 1860: California quail released near Victoria. 1912: first Okanagan record, 70 percent. 1950s: chukar released in BC. 1970s: BC quail harvest up to 4,600 birds. 1970 to 2012: breeding bird survey trend up, low reliability. 2008 to 2012: the atlas finds the Fraser Valley population apparently gone. Recent harvest under 1,000 a year, 65 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail and chukar in BC: a short history</text>\n<line x1=\"30\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"256\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"40\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">1860</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Quail released near Victoria</text>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"82\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"87\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">1912</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"87\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">First Okanagan record (70%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"124\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">1950s</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Chukar released in BC</text>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"166\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">1970s</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">BC quail harvest up to 4,600</text>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"208\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">1970 to 2012</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Quail count trend up (low reliability)</text>\n<circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"250\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">2008 to 2012</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Atlas: Fraser Valley birds gone</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recent harvest: under 1,000 a year (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Introduced to BC between 1860 and 1912 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Two main areas: the Okanagan and Kettle valleys, and southeast Vancouver Island <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: history, numbers and trend</summary><ul><li>California quail were released on the coast and in the southern Interior between 1860 and 1912, from a native range in California and Baja California (85%, BC Breeding Bird Atlas).</li><li>Earliest Okanagan record: 1912 (70%, Lewin 1965, The Condor, search preview). The Okanagan birds may also have come north from releases in northern Washington (60%, iNFOnews).</li><li>The atlas (2008 to 2012) found the Fraser Valley population apparently gone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. So no quail near Mission.</li><li>Breeding Bird Survey trend for BC, 1970 to 2012: up about 5.8% a year, low reliability (85% that this is what the atlas reports).</li><li>The increase comes mostly from Interior birds; coastal birds are doing less well <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>BC quail harvest: up to 4,600 birds in the 1970s, under 1,000 a year recently (65%, BC Outdoors 2021).</li><li>Conservation status: not at risk <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Chukar: released in the south central Interior in the 1950s; best on low slopes of the Thompson from Kamloops to Lytton, also the South Okanagan and Similkameen (65%, BC Outdoors and KnowBC).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Grid of six birds, legal or not, from the app Rule Book. California quail, curled plume: yes, Region 8. Mountain quail, straight plume: no open season. Chukar, red bill and black necklace: yes, Regions 3 and 8. Gray partridge, orange face: yes, Regions 3 and 8. Pheasant cock, green head and white ring: yes, cocks only. Pheasant hen, brown with a long tail: never. 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Legal or not? From the Rule Book</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"36\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">California quail</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Curled plume</text>\n<rect x=\"34\" y=\"86\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, Region 8</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"36\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mountain quail</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Straight plume</text>\n<rect x=\"226\" y=\"86\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO season</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"113\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red bill, necklace</text>\n<rect x=\"34\" y=\"163\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, Regions 3, 8</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"113\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gray partridge</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange face</text>\n<rect x=\"226\" y=\"163\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, Regions 3, 8</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"190\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pheasant cock</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Green head, ring</text>\n<rect x=\"34\" y=\"240\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#3f7f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">YES, cocks only</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"190\" width=\"184\" height=\"72\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pheasant hen</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brown, long tail</text>\n<rect x=\"226\" y=\"240\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NEVER</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Seasons: Rule Book (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Curl is legal, straight is not; ring on the cock, or hold your shot.\" (Tip)</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> \"2, 4, 6\": quail about 200 g, Hun about 400 g, chukar about 600 g (75%, rounded).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Face code:</strong> black face = cock quail; orange face = Hun; black necklace = chukar (75 to 80%).</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"Name it in the air or let it go.\" Hunting educators teach positive ID before every shot (Tip).</li><li><strong>Date hook:</strong> quail came to BC between 1860 and 1912: \"sixty to twelve\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>BC Breeding Bird Atlas, Audubon, Okanagan and BC Outdoors articles, the app Rule Book. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.birdatlas.bc.ca/accounts/speciesaccount.jsp?sp=CAQU&amp;lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Breeding Bird Atlas, California quail account (Starzomski 2015)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: introduction dates, range, elevation, plume, coveys, trend, status <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/california-quail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Audubon field guide: California quail</a>, <a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/chukar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chukar</a>, <a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/gray-partridge\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gray partridge</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: sizes, weights, marks, calls <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://friendsofedgewood.org/?p=5231\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Friends of Edgewood: California quail (Franks 2002, from Calkins et al. 1999, Birds of North America)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: male and female marks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bcoutdoorsmagazine.com/?p=9278\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Outdoors: California quail (Harris 2021)</a> and <a href=\"https://www.bcoutdoorsmagazine.com/chukar-asian-partridge-made-a-home-for-itself-in-bc/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chukar (Harris 2019)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: weight, harvest, chukar in BC <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://infonews.ca/?p=13774\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">iNFOnews: quail in the Southern Interior (2018)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Lewin, V. 1965. The introduction and present status of California quail in the Okanagan Valley of British Columbia. The Condor 67: 61 to 66. <a href=\"https://digitalcommons.usf.edu/condor/vol67/iss1/5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Record</a>, search preview only 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Aging: Condor 1963 California quail aging study (search preview) and <a href=\"https://projectupland.com/quail-subspecies/determining-the-age-of-a-quail-from-wing-feathers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Project Upland: age a quail from wing feathers</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 (60 to 70%).</li><li>Rules: the app <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Rule Book, Region 8</a> and the <a href=\"#/s/upland-birds\">quick lesson</a>, BC synopsis 2026 to 2028, 2 October 2026 edition, pages 21 and 68 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Photos: Wikimedia Commons, credits under each photo.</li></ul></details>"]